+Jointly available Data ACK and credit MAY share one bounded publication and
+protected transport write. They remain two independently meaningful wire
+frames; sharing a record creates no decoding dependency or combined receipt/
+credit authority. Neither kind may wait for the other to become available.
+In particular, a non-blocking local delivery attempt may make credit available
+alongside receipt, but pending or failed delivery MUST NOT postpone receipt
+publication or required startup/lifecycle service. A partial write is retained,
+not replayed, and does not authorize unconsumed credit. Successful queue
+admission advances only the exact ACK chunk and grant it accepted; completing
+an ACK generation still requires all of its chunks. An already-covered ACK
+or blocked catch-up MUST NOT prevent independent credit publication and retry.
+The two frames retain their full accounting and terminal ownership through
+native write/flush completion or cleanup. This adds no feedback timer, batching
+threshold, larger receive window, or preferred return carrier.
+
